  },
  {
    id: "cert",
    name: "Certificates and SPIFFE",
    tone: "green",
    question: "How do two workloads prove themselves to each other?",
    body: "Two routes to an X.509 identity. With **Pod Certificates**, the kubelet generates a key, files a PodCertificateRequest with a signer, and mounts the result. With **SPIRE**, a node agent attests the calling process over a local socket and hands it a SPIFFE certificate. Either way the workload gets a short-lived certificate, usually carrying a SPIFFE ID, and a trust bundle to verify peers.",
